.TH SCAN-REALITY 1 "October 2026" "scripts" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scan-reality \- high-performance asynchronous TLS 1.3 & HTTP/2 camouflage scanner for XTLS Reality
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scan-reality
[\fB\-w\fR \fIPATH_OR_URL\fR]
[\fB\-o\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR \fBcsv\fR|\fBjson\fR|\fBtxt\fR]
[\fB\-c\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fISEC\fR]
[\fB\-\-no-h2\fR]
[\fB\-\-allow-redirects\fR]
[\fB\-\-allow-status\fR \fICODES\fR]
[\fB\-\-allow-untrusted-cert\fR]
[\fB\-\-top\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR]
[\fB\-\-verbose\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
[\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBscan-reality\fR is an asynchronous reconnaissance and validation utility engineered to identify and rank high-speed, legitimate camouflage domains for \fBXTLS Reality\fR (VLESS Reality).
.PP
Unlike naive ICMP ping utilities (which fail against bank and government servers that drop ICMP echo requests) or opaque compiled binaries, \fBscan-reality\fR performs direct multi-stage network diagnostics:
.IP 1. 4
\fBDNS Resolution:\fR Resolves domain hostnames to IPv4 endpoints.
.IP 2. 4
\fBTCP Handshake (RTT):\fR Connects to port 443 and measures raw TCP round-trip latency.
.IP 3. 4
\fBTLS 1.3 Handshake:\fR Enforces TLSv1.3 negotiation, verifies ALPN (\fBh2\fR), inspects the X.509 certificate trust chain, validates Subject Alternative Names (SAN), and measures TLS handshake latency.
.IP 4. 4
\fBHTTP/2 Probing:\fR Dispatches an HTTP GET request to verify server status (defaulting to 200 OK) and detects external 3xx redirects to eliminate DPI camouflage anomalies.
.PP
Survivors are sorted ascending by total connection latency (\fBTCP RTT + TLS Handshake + HTTP TTFB\fR) and exported to CSV, JSON, or plain text lists.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-w " PATH_OR_URL" "\fR, \fB\-\-whitelist" " PATH_OR_URL"
Path to a local domain list, an HTTP(S) URL to fetch remotely, or \fB\-\fR to read from standard input. If omitted, the utility uses an embedded curated whitelist of stable Russian domestic services (VK, Mail.ru, Yandex, 2GIS, Ozon, etc.).
.TP
.BI \-o " PATH" "\fR, \fB\-\-output" " PATH"
Destination file path. Defaults to \fBreality_targets_YYYY-MM-DD.csv\fR in the current working directory.
.TP
.BI \-f " FORMAT" "\fR, \fB\-\-format" " FORMAT"
Output serialization format: \fBcsv\fR (default), \fBjson\fR, or \fBtxt\fR (one domain per line).
.TP
.BI \-c " N" "\fR, \fB\-\-concurrency" " N"
Number of concurrent asynchronous scan workers. Defaults to \fB40\fR.
.TP
.BI \-t " SEC" "\fR, \fB\-\-timeout" " SEC"
Network timeout in seconds per host connection and handshake attempt. Defaults to \fB4.0\fR seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-no-h2
Do not strictly require ALPN \fBh2\fR (allows HTTP/1.1 fallback).
.TP
.B \-\-allow-redirects
Permit HTTP 301, 302, 307, or 308 redirects. By default, any redirect is rejected.
.TP
.BI \-\-allow-status " CODES"
Comma-separated list of acceptable HTTP response status codes. Defaults to \fB200\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-untrusted-cert
Bypass strict X.509 certificate trust chain validation. Useful when scanning environments containing custom internal roots or Russian Trusted Root CAs (Минцифры).
.TP
.BI \-\-top " N"
Number of top fastest candidates to preview in the terminal summary. Defaults to \fB5\fR (set to \fB0\fR to disable preview).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode. Suppresses the real-time interactive terminal progress bar.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Prints failure diagnostics for rejected domains to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print version number and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B 1. Scan default curated domestic whitelist:
scan-reality
.TP
.B 2. Scan custom domain list and output JSON:
scan-reality -w /path/to/whitelist.txt -o reality.json -f json
.TP
.B 3. High-concurrency scan with top 10 preview:
scan-reality -w whitelist.txt -c 100 -t 3.0 --top 10
.TP
.B 4. Pipeline execution via standard input:
cat candidate_domains.txt | scan-reality -w - -o fastest.csv
.TP
.B 5. Scan remote whitelist URL directly:
scan-reality -w https://raw.githubusercontent.com/user/repo/main/whitelist.txt
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xray (1),
.BR sing-box (1)
